title No proxy decides this, so the loom asks the file
prompt The card handed BAKERY a loom -- two greps read the count-in-front-of-a-byte-ceiling class in every module, and a second firing asks for one guard rather than another ledger row.
rota lap 4506, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; its own test is to press a claimed boundary and write down where the hand passes through, which is what happened to four discriminators in a row and became the guard's design rather than its footnote
think Read Diffuser's paper first. It walked mantra, caravan, tally, aurora by hand -- 177 sources, 4 candidates, 2 real, 2 false -- and named its own reach: Glow, Skate, Kumara and the crypto rungs stand outside it.
think Checked for an existing guard before building. tools/d/declared_ceiling_witness.rish is rostered under a near-identical name and reads PAGES -- Ceiling headers and living_pin_max_bytes -- so the code-side reading was genuinely unbuilt.
think Reproduced the census tree-wide: 48 candidate files against the paper's 4, twelve times the population a hand could walk.
think Then tried to mechanize the judgment, four times, and every proxy leaked. Names in one function admits recall_lap1, where append_leaf checks leaf_count and content.len three lines apart with no arithmetic between them. Byte name checked after a loop admits glow_storage_scope, a per-item length check inside a loop over entries. Byte name checked against a variable that loop advances admits it again, on a partial match against a struct field.
think The real test is whether the loop ACCUMULATES into the buffer the byte ceiling bounds -- an offset advanced per item and asserted at the end. That is dataflow, not text. A guard that guessed would red on honest work and get turned off.
think So the design changed: the loom stops judging and asks the file to declare, which is exactly what declared_ceiling does for a page and tutorial_output for a command. Where a judgment cannot be mechanized, mechanize the declaration of it.
think Two of my own boundaries gave way while building, and both are penned now. A pattern ending at [0-9]+ read `= 8 * session.max_samples` as a literal 8 and admitted nine derived ceilings -- the precise shape the guard exists to reward. And comlink/ holds symlinks into mantra/, so the census counted recall_sync_wire.rye twice and reported six instances where the tree holds four.
obs A derived ceiling leaves the population by construction, since the pattern demands a bare literal as the whole right-hand side. So the repair is rewarded by the reading rather than merely permitted, and caravan/ -- whose rung bounds are chained, max_finding_bytes = max_referral_bytes + 1 -- is absent from the census for the right reason.
obs One gate, two ratchets, and the split is deliberate. The gate is an unreadable verdict, at zero: a declaration no tool can read is indistinguishable from no declaration, which is how docs/CRYPTO.md drifted past its own ceiling for months. Both ratchets only fall, because a wall over 29 undeclared files would refuse every module on the seating lap.
obs The first cut ran 26 seconds -- two greps per file across 1,964 sources, where 1,935 leave the population on the first pattern. declared_ceiling booked this same arithmetic on 20260907. Batched to two greps total: 1.4s, same reading.
obs Found and not taken: mantra_recall_catch_up_wire and mantra_recall_batch_wire red at their DEVICE leg, rev2 catch-up RED. Both build clean and their hosted selftests read GREEN, so my comment-only edits are not the cause -- git diff reads 15 insertions, every one a // line, zero deletions. Neither is rostered. Patchouli's lane; named rather than guessed at.
obs The card sat at 40,850 of 40,960. The block landed by tightening four times rather than by raising the bound: 1,767 bytes drafted, 1,469 shipped, card at 40,957.
